// SHPFFIL - Hello World! :: RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   colour     : not assigned by Linguist
//   layer      : full (byte-balanced rainbow bar)
//   upstream   : https://github.com/quxianp/RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   reference  : see https://esolangs.org/ and https://rosettacode.org/

// SHPFFIL: the attribute table that sits beside a shapefile --
// a .dbf, in dBASE III.
//
// A dBASE table has eleven bytes per field name and that is the
// whole of its free-text budget, so `Hello World!` gets the ten
// characters that fit. The date in bytes 2-4 is there because the
// format requires it, and the header ends with a 0x0D.
//
// shpffil: 76 bytes, dumped sixteen at a time.
//
// The bytes below are not hand-written. They are built from the
// format's own field widths by scripts/build_object_formats.py, and
// scripts/verify_encodings.py reads the fields back by name -- the
// magic number, the lengths, the offsets. A hex dump written from
// memory is wrong in one byte and looks exactly like a correct one.
//

// 03 7E 01 01 00 00 00 00 41 00 0C 00 00 00 00 00 |.~......A.......|   <- 0000
// 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 |................|   <- 0010
// 48 65 6C 6C 6F 57 6F 72 6C 64 00 43 00 00 00 00 |HelloWorld.C....|   <- 0020
// 0B 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 |................|   <- 0030
// 0D 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20             |.           |   <- 0040
